4. Subjects who are able to comply with protocol-specified requirements;
5. Subjects with negative urine pregnancy test result at screening;
6. Subjects with no childbearing potential (e.g. females who have undergone bilateral tubal ligation, hysterectomy, bilateral oophorectomy, etc), or subjects with childbearing potential who have agreed to abstain from any sexual activity that could result in pregnancy or practice adequate contraception for at least 28 days prior to the first dose and throughout the study;
